<title>UK: De Beers diamond sales up seven pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>De Beers diamond sales up seven pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diamond giant De Beers said rough diamond sales by its Central Selling Organisation rose seven percent to $4.834 billion in 1996 from $4.531 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that sales in the second half of the year were $2.09 billion, up five percent on the same period in 1995.</p>
</text>
